@startuml agent-start-states
' cumin works - the state of cumin itself for the starts of agents (quota). the quota transitions of issue-states.md
' are transitions of this machine, not of an issue.
' Render: run scripts/render-diagrams.sh at the root of the repository.

hide empty description

state "starting agents" as Starting
Starting : do / cumin starts the agent of each transition\nthat requests work

state "agent starts stopped" as Stopped
Stopped : do / cumin lets the runs that go on end,\nand starts no agent. Every issue keeps its state

[*] --> Starting
Starting --> Stopped : stop agent starts\n[cumin reads a quota window at its limit,\nor cannot read the usage]\n/ cumin notifies the Owner
Stopped --> Starting : resume agent starts\nthe Owner allows the 5h window\n[the weekly window is under its limit]
Stopped --> Starting : resume agent starts\n[the time of cumin's next try passed,\nboth windows are under their limit]

note "tell the Owner that cumin waits, in both states: [nothing can go on without the Owner,\nno agent runs, no issue waits only for the quota] / cumin tells the Owner once that it waits." as Q4

legend right
  This machine has one instance for one cumin, not one for each issue.
  It lives on the Host (the latest quota reading of cumin), not on GitHub.
  While agent starts are stopped, cumin still takes every transition that starts no agent
  (a label, a comment, a notification, a merge, a close).
endlegend

@enduml
